# Since Timer App � Claude Code Build Guide

## Recommended Stack
| Layer | Choice | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| Framework | Expo (React Native) | Cross-platform iOS/Android, easy setup |
| Language | TypeScript | Type safety for entry/category models |
| Storage | SQLite via `expo-sqlite` | Persistent local DB, works offline |
| Notifications | `expo-notifications` | Native push/local reminder alerts |
| Navigation | Expo Router (file-based) | Simple tab + stack navigation |
| UI | React Native Paper | Material design, ready-made components |
| Date handling | `date-fns` | Lightweight, no overhead |

---

## Phase 1 � Project Setup

```
Prompt to Claude Code:
```

> Create a new Expo project with TypeScript called `since-timer`. 
Install dependencies: `expo-sqlite`, `expo-notifications`, `expo-router`, `react-native-paper`, `date-fns`. 
Set up an Expo Router layout with two tabs: **Home** (entry list) and **Add Entry**. 
Configure app.json with notification permissions for iOS and Android.

---

## Phase 2 � Database Schema

```
Prompt:
```

> Create a SQLite database module at `lib/db.ts`. Define and initialise these tables on app launch:
>
> **entries** table:
> - `id` INTEGER PRIMARY KEY
> - `title` TEXT NOT NULL
> - `category` TEXT � values: `purchase | task | event | routine`
> - `entry_date` TEXT (ISO format)
> - `next_due_date` TEXT (nullable)
> - `price` REAL (nullable)
> - `notes` TEXT (nullable)
> - `reminder_enabled` INTEGER (0/1)
> - `created_at` TEXT
>
> **history** table:
> - `id` INTEGER PRIMARY KEY
> - `entry_id` INTEGER (FK ? entries)
> - `logged_date` TEXT
> - `notes` TEXT
>
> Add a setting in an **app_settings** table: `history_months` INTEGER DEFAULT 6.
> Expose typed CRUD functions: `insertEntry`, `getAllEntries`, `updateEntry`, `deleteEntry`, `getHistoryForEntry`, `pruneOldHistory(months)`.

---

## Phase 3 � Data Model & Types

```
Prompt:
```

> Create `types/entry.ts` with TypeScript interfaces matching the DB schema. 
Include a helper type `TimeSummary` with fields: `daysPassed: number`, `weeksPassed: number`, 
`monthsPassed: number`, `nextDueIn: number | null`, `isOverdue: boolean`. 
Create a utility `lib/timeUtils.ts` using `date-fns` that computes `TimeSummary` 
from an entry's `entry_date` and `next_due_date`.

---

## Phase 4 � Home Screen (Entry List)

```
Prompt:
```

> Build `app/(tabs)/index.tsx` as the Home screen. It should:
> - Load all entries from SQLite on mount
> - Show each entry as a card displaying: title, category badge, time since (e.g. "14 days ago"), next due countdown or overdue warning, price (if set)
> - Add filter chips at the top for category: All / Purchase / Task / Event / Routine
> - Tapping a card opens an Entry Detail screen
> - Pull-to-refresh to reload
> - Show an empty state with a prompt to add the first entry

---

## Phase 5 � Add / Edit Entry Screen

```
Prompt:
```

> Build `app/add-entry.tsx` and reuse it for editing. Form fields:
> - Title (text input)
> - Category (segmented buttons: Purchase / Task / Event / Routine)
> - Entry Date (date picker, defaults to today)
> - Next Due Date (optional date picker)
> - Price (optional numeric input, shown only for Purchase category)
> - Notes (optional multiline)
> - Reminder toggle � if enabled, show a time picker for the reminder time
>
> On save: insert/update SQLite, schedule a local notification if reminder is on. Validate that title and entry date are filled.

---

## Phase 6 � Entry Detail & History Screen

```
Prompt:
```

> Build `app/entry/[id].tsx`. Display:
> - Full entry info and live `TimeSummary`
> - A **Log Again** button (re-records the event as of today, adds previous date to history table)
> - History list � past logged dates with notes, respecting the `history_months` setting
> - Edit and Delete actions in the header
> - For purchases: show total spend if logged multiple times

---

## Phase 7 � Notifications

```
Prompt:
```

> In `lib/notifications.ts`, implement:
> - `requestPermissions()` � call on first launch
> - `scheduleReminder(entry)` � schedules a local notification on `next_due_date` at user-chosen time; notification body: "Time to log: {title}"
> - `cancelReminder(entryId)` � cancels existing notification for that entry
> - `rescheduleAll(entries)` � used on app resume to refresh all active reminders
> Hook these into insert/update/delete flows.

---

## Phase 8 � Settings Screen

```
Prompt:
```

> Add a Settings tab at `app/(tabs)/settings.tsx` with:
> - **History retention**: slider or dropdown � 1 / 3 / 6 / 12 months. On change, call `pruneOldHistory(months)` and save to `app_settings`.
> - **Notification permission status** with a re-request button
> - **Export data** button � serialise all entries + history to a JSON file and share via `expo-sharing`
> - **About** section showing app version

---

## Phase 9 � Polish & Edge Cases

```
Prompt:
```

> Review the full app and add:
> 1. Overdue highlight � entries past `next_due_date` shown in red/amber
> 2. Sort options on Home: by date added, by most overdue, by category
> 3. On cold app launch, call `rescheduleAll()` to restore any lost notifications
> 4. Confirm dialog before deleting an entry
> 5. Keyboard-aware scroll on the Add Entry form
> 6. Dark mode support using React Native Paper theming

---

## Suggested Claude Code Session Flow

1. Run phases 1�3 in one session (foundation)
2. Run phases 4�5 next (core UI)
3. Run phases 6�7 (detail + notifications)
4. Run phases 8�9 last (settings + polish)

> **Tip:** Start each session by showing Claude Code the current file tree and any errors � it will self-correct without re-doing work.
